  "data": {
    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "10. Shooting Phase",
    "ruleNumber": "10.06",
    "summary": "An engaged unit that has not Advanced this turn can shoot this way if it has at least one [CLOSE-QUARTERS] weapon or is itself a MONSTER/VEHICLE unit. Its models are allowed to target enemy units their unit is engaged with. For each attack by a MONSTER/VEHICLE model, the Hit roll takes -1 unless the attack uses a [CLOSE-QUARTERS] weapon against a unit engaged with the firer's unit, and a [BLAST] weapon still may not target any unit engaged with the firer's unit. Every other model is limited to [CLOSE-QUARTERS] weapons and to targets engaged with its unit. Attacks follow Making Attacks (04), and for the rest of the phase the unit may not begin an Action.",
